INT. LAKEVIEW BANQUET HALL - WEDDING AFTERPARTY - NIGHT

Streamers. Half-eaten cake. A DJ plays something slow to a nearly empty floor. A WAITER carries a tray of champagne flutes between tables. Two TEENAGERS in matching rented suits hide behind a pillar, sharing a vape. A small WHITE DOG in a bow tie trots under the head table, hunting for crumbs.

At a corner table, NORA, 28, bridesmaid, grips her clutch. Across from her sits CALLUM, 30s, the groom's cousin, loosening his tie.

NORA
(low, smiling for the room)
Don't look at the bar.

CALLUM
(looking at the bar)
Which one is he?

NORA
(sips water)
Grey suit. Left of the cake.

CALLUM
(squints)
That's the best man.

NORA
That's not the best man.

A beat. The Waiter passes. Nora lifts a flute. Sets it down untouched.

DEVON arrives, 30s, the real best man, grinning, a bit sweaty, and slides into the chair next to Callum.

DEVON
(clapping Callum on the shoulder)
There you are! Where were you during the toast?

CALLUM
(stiff)
Parking.

DEVON
(to Nora)
And you owe me a dance.

NORA
(too bright)
Later.

DEVON
(leaning in)
You okay? You look pale.

NORA
(squeezing the clutch)
Long day.

The Dog yips under the table. One of the Teenagers giggles. The other shushes him.

MARIN, 50s, the bride's mother in a silver dress, glides up behind them.

MARIN
(tapping Devon's arm)
Dev, the photographer needs you. Now.

DEVON
(rising, to Callum)
Don't leave. We're doing shots at midnight.

He goes. Marin lingers, her eyes on Nora.

MARIN
(softly)
He is lovely, isn't he?

NORA
(nodding, tight)
Very.

MARIN
(turning to Callum)
And you. You'll keep an eye on her?

CALLUM
(a beat)
Yes, ma'am.

Marin smiles and drifts away. Nora exhales. Callum turns to her.

CALLUM (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Your clutch. What's in it?

NORA
(eyes on the dance floor)
Not here.

The DJ fades out the slow song. The room claps, thinly. The Waiter returns for the flute Nora never touched. She hands it to him with a smile that does not reach her eyes.
